WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200
Speaker 1: Welcome to the David Pakman show. I am&nbsp;
Farren Cousins sitting in for David Pakman today.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.880
And you know what? We've got a lot to talk&nbsp;
about, so let's just hop right into it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:16.720
First and foremost, let's talk about the midterms,&nbsp;
because we do have a very important day coming up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:24.240
very soon, and that is Labor Day. And typically in&nbsp;
election years, once you hit that Labor Day mark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:33.600
everybody switches into general election mode.&nbsp;
So if you're already tired of midterm news,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.200
then I am very sorry because there is going to&nbsp;
be a lot coming out once we hit Labor Day in just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:45.680
a couple of weeks here. But right now and this&nbsp;
honestly is super astonishing. I love to see it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:52.000
though, Democrats are looking pretty good,&nbsp;
right? Generic ballot polling actually has them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.200
up against Republicans in House races. The&nbsp;
Senate now looks like it's firmly going to be in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:04.560
Democratic control. To the point where we may not&nbsp;
even have to worry about people like Joe Manchin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:11.600
or Kirsten Cinema for the next two years, things&nbsp;
are looking pretty darn good. You've got the post&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:18.960
Roe bump, you've got the Inflation Reduction Act.&nbsp;
Gas prices are coming down. Inflation coming down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:26.720
a little still really bad. Unemployment numbers&nbsp;
look good on paper. But there is one thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:35.440
Republicans have going for them right now, and&nbsp;
that, of course, is Donald Trump's post FBI raid.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:44.800
Pull bounce. Now, I use the term raid not because&nbsp;
I'm, you know, agreeing it was a raid, but because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.800
that's a lot easier than saying the FBI's&nbsp;
execution of the search warrant at Mar a Lago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:54.240
So please understand when I use the word raid,&nbsp;
what I mean is the lawful execution of the search&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:02:01.360
warrant down at Mar a Lago. But his poll numbers&nbsp;
have gotten a bounce from that. And, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:08.080
Ron DeSantis, his poll numbers have actually&nbsp;
gone down since the FBI went down to Mar a Lago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:16.480
And if that Republican anger holds. Republicans&nbsp;
may do better in this year's midterm elections,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:23.840
or at least that's the prevailing theory. Right.&nbsp;
We have seen Republicans postulate this. Cassidy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:29.040
Hutchinson, of course, who was one of the star&nbsp;
witnesses of the January six committee over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:35.240
summer, came out the day after and said, Well,&nbsp;
you just handed the midterms to the Republicans. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:41.840
don't agree. KC There's a big difference.&nbsp;
What's happening with the Democrats right now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:52.000
is that you have anger over Roe versus Wade&nbsp;
getting overturned. You have anger at January 6th.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:59.680
You have the lingering threat of authoritarianism&nbsp;
coming from all of these Republican controlled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:07.280
states, taking away rights of certain groups&nbsp;
of individuals state by state. All of that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:15.360
has angered Democratic voters, but more&nbsp;
importantly, it has energized them. Compare that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:22.240
to what's on the other side. Oh, we're so mad at&nbsp;
the FBI right now. Cool. You're going to be mad in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:28.480
a week. You're going to be mad in two weeks.&nbsp;
And by the way, the funniest part about that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:34.400
is a lot of that anger already had subsided and&nbsp;
not saying all of it did, because you still have,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:39.680
you know, the people out there threatening&nbsp;
the lives of FBI agents, threatening the lives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:43.840
of Merrick Garland and other members of&nbsp;
the DOJ, the magistrate judge Reinhart.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:52.800
But. The anger had already started to subside by&nbsp;
the time we learned that Donald Trump likely had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.800 --> 00:04:01.040
classified nuclear documents down there at Mar a&nbsp;
Lago. Majority of independents support the raid.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:06.400
Majority of Democrats obviously do. Republicans&nbsp;
only about half. Right, and I think 50%.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:17.520
Are opposed to the raid. So even if the&nbsp;
Republicans, by virtue of Trump got a bounce in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:24.160
the polls, which Trump did, I don't know that that&nbsp;
anger carries. Right. You've got the front page,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:29.120
the cover story really of Newsweek right&nbsp;
now talking about this post-trade bounce.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:35.520
Is this enough to push Republicans over&nbsp;
the edge? No. No, it isn't. Not even close,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:40.640
because the more that comes out about&nbsp;
it, the worse it looks for Donald Trump.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:45.840
Now, I will give Trump credit, which is not&nbsp;
something I ever do, but I will give him credit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:52.320
last week for kind of backing the DOJ into&nbsp;
a corner by calling for the release of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:56.800
affidavit. You know, let us see all the evidence&nbsp;
you have, including the name of the leaker.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.320
So that we can clear all this up with the public.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:06.400
Well, whoever was advising him to do that&nbsp;
clearly understood that the DOJ can't do that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:13.040
You know, not only would they put lives&nbsp;
unnecessarily at risk, because we've all seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:19.200
the threats coming from Trump supporters, but it&nbsp;
also could impede the actual investigation itself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:26.000
If we release this, you'd get the names&nbsp;
of individuals cooperating. You might get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:31.280
the names of other targets. You might get more&nbsp;
information that could lead to the destruction of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:39.760
evidence. And we cannot do that. In fact, the DOJ&nbsp;
actually came out within the last couple of days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:44.320
and admitted part of the reason we don't&nbsp;
want to release this is actually to protect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:51.440
you, Donald Trump. But the reason I say&nbsp;
that that kind of backed the DOJ into a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:54.640
corner is because Trump called for the&nbsp;
release. He knew they couldn't do it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.520 --> 00:06:01.920
So once they say, No, we can't. He goes, Aha,&nbsp;
I gotcha. I knew all this was phony, otherwise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:07.120
you'd release it. And his supporters, including,&nbsp;
you know, plenty of people in right wing media,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.640
also jumped on that messaging,&nbsp;
saying, obviously it's fake.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:17.760
And the reason they're jumping on that messaging&nbsp;
is because they want to get that bounce back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:23.520
They want to make sure that those positive&nbsp;
poll developments that they have seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:27.680
since the search on Mar a Lago, they want to&nbsp;
make sure that they hold on to the midterms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:33.840
So they want to keep talking about it because they&nbsp;
think it's going to help Republicans in November.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:40.560
But in reality, what it's going to do is it's&nbsp;
further going to energize Democrats and it's going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:46.800
to turn independents away from the Republican&nbsp;
Party. So they're stuck between a rock and a hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:51.680
place, right? They want to talk about it because&nbsp;
they think it helps with the Republican base.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:56.800
But at the same time, the more they talk about&nbsp;
it, the more it's going to turn off independents.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:03.680
Neither party in this country can win&nbsp;
elections, maybe win some primaries, obviously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:10.160
but you can't win a general&nbsp;
election. If you do not attract those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:16.080
middle of the road, moderate, independent voters,&nbsp;
you simply cannot. The numbers are not there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:23.280
So the more Republicans talk about it, the worst&nbsp;
their poll numbers ultimately are going to get.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:29.600
They may have gotten that little bitty bounce&nbsp;
right now, but it's not a type of anger that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:35.760
sustainable. Certainly not in a year when&nbsp;
Trump isn't even on the ballot. You know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:43.040
if this was 2024 and this happened and Trump was&nbsp;
running, that would help all Republicans. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:48.240
he's not on the ballot this year. So I don't&nbsp;
know what the Republican strategy here is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:55.760
but I do know with pretty much certainty&nbsp;
that it definitely is not working for them.

